{"_meta":{"source":"Yahoo Finance via yfinance (profile, statements, analyst estimates)","fetched_at":"2026-10-29T07:37:38+00:00","status":"ok","error":null,"last_success":"2026-10-29T07:37:38+00:00"},"data":{"profile":{"name":"Apple Inc.","sector":"Technology","industry":"Consumer Electronics","country":"United States","city":"Cupertino","website":"https://www.apple.com","employees":150000,"summary":"Apple Inc. designs, manufactures, and markets smartphones, personal computers, tablets, wearables, and accessories worldwide. The company offers iPhone, a line of smartphones; Mac, a line of personal computers; iPad, a line of multi-purpose tablets; and wearables, home, and accessories comprising AirPods, Apple Vision Pro, Apple TV, Apple Watch, Beats products, and HomePod, as well as Apple branded and third-party accessories. It also provides AppleCare support and cloud services; and operates various platforms, including the App Store that allows customers to discover and download applications and digital content, such as books, music, video, games, and podcasts, as well as advertising services include third-party licensing arrangements and its own advertising platforms. In addition, the company offers various subscription-based services, such as Apple Arcade, a game subscription service; Apple Fitness+, a personalized fitness service; Apple Music, which offers users a curated listening experience with on-demand radio stations; Apple News+, a subscription news and magazine service; Apple TV, which offers original content and live sports; Apple Card, a co-branded credit card; and Apple Pay, a cashless payment service, as well as licenses its intellectual property. The company serves consumers, and small and mid-sized businesses; and the education, enterprise, and government markets. It distributes third-party applications for its products through the App Store. The company also sells its products through its retail and online stores, and direct sales force; and third-party cellular network carriers and resellers. The company was formerly known as Apple Computer, Inc. and changed its name to Apple Inc. in January 2007. Apple Inc. was founded in 1976 and is headquartered in Cupertino, California.","exchange":"NasdaqGS","currency":"USD","financial_currency":"USD","summary_fr":"Apple Inc. conçoit, fabrique et commercialise des smartphones, des ordinateurs personnels, des tablettes, des appareils portables et des accessoires dans le monde entier. La société propose iPhone, une gamme de smartphones; Mac, une gamme d'ordinateurs personnels; iPad, une gamme de tablettes multifonctions; et wearables, maison, et accessoires comprenant AirPods, Apple Vision Pro, Apple TV, Apple Watch, produits Beats, et HomePod, ainsi que des accessoires de marque Apple et tiers. Il fournit également un support AppleCare et des services cloud ; et exploite diverses plateformes, y compris l’App Store qui permet aux clients de découvrir et de télécharger des applications et du contenu numérique, tels que des livres, de la musique, des vidéos, des jeux et des podcasts, ainsi que des services publicitaires, notamment des accords de licence tiers et ses propres plateformes publicitaires. En outre, la société propose divers services par abonnement, tels que Apple Arcade, un service d’abonnement de jeux; Apple Fitness +, un service de remise en forme personnalisé; Apple Music, qui offre aux utilisateurs une expérience d’écoute organisée avec des stations de radio à la demande; Apple News +, un service d’actualités et de magazines par abonnement; Apple TV, qui offre du contenu original et des sports en direct; Apple Card, une carte de crédit co-marque; et Apple Pay, un service de paiement sans espèces. La société sert les consommateurs et les petites et moyennes entreprises; et les marchés de l'éducation, des entreprises et du gouvernement. Elle distribue des applications tierces pour ses produits via l’App Store. La société vend également ses produits par le biais de ses magasins de détail et de ses magasins en ligne, de sa force de vente directe et de ses fournisseurs et revendeurs de réseaux cellulaires tiers. La société était auparavant connue sous le nom d’Apple Computer, Inc. et a changé son nom pour Apple Inc. en janvier 2007. Apple Inc. a été fondée en 1976 et a son siège social à Cupertino, en Californie."},"valuation":{"market_cap_yahoo":5017916932096,"shares_outstanding":14594180000,"trailing_pe":39.430042,"forward_pe":35.956264,"price_to_book":46.71603,"ev_to_ebitda":30.007,"ev_to_revenue":10.796,"dividend_yield":0.0031,"payout_ratio":0.1204,"beta_yahoo":1.069},"targets":{"current_price":343.83,"mean":332.3858,"median":337.5,"high":405.0,"low":245.0,"n_analysts":38,"reco_mean":2.25,"reco_key":"buy"},"calendar":{"earnings_dates":["2026-11-02"],"eps_avg":1.98261,"eps_low":1.93,"eps_high":2.06,"revenue_avg":113322287400,"ex_dividend":"2026-08-10","dividend_date":"2026-08-13"},"holders":{"insiders_pct":0.01648,"institutions_pct":0.66352,"institutions_float_pct":0.67463994,"institutions_n":7711,"institutions":[{"name":"Blackrock Inc.","pct":0.0797,"shares":1162996939,"value":399873221919,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.016},{"name":"Vanguard Capital Management LLC","pct":0.0657,"shares":959107911,"value":329770060160,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0055},{"name":"State Street Corporation","pct":0.0421,"shares":615129929,"value":211500115228,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0212},{"name":"Geode Capital Management, LLC","pct":0.0254,"shares":371336543,"value":127676638593,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0074},{"name":"Vanguard Portfolio Management LLC","pct":0.0229,"shares":334119156,"value":114880184921,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0081},{"name":"FMR, LLC","pct":0.0223,"shares":325348754,"value":111864657719,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0582},{"name":"Morgan Stanley","pct":0.0166,"shares":242614238,"value":83418050193,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":-0.0076},{"name":"JPMORGAN CHASE & CO","pct":0.015700001,"shares":228762008,"value":78655238138,